516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (While recent research in China demonstrates that cultural tightness undermines SCC, little attention has been given to whether the same effect extends to South Asia, specifically India, where tightness is reinforced because of emic features such as caste norms and family obligations \(Mo et al., 2025; Sahakari, 2024\). It is also unclear how moderate-tight societies like India compare with loose cultures beyond the United States. Canada provides a meaningful loose contrast because its normative environment is shaped by unique features such as legally institutionalised multiculturalism, high immigrant population and strong provincial autonomy \(Brink, 2023; Uz, 2014\). By comparing India and Canada, this study investigates how variations in cultural tightness shape SCC in two distinct, understudied contexts.)
/Pg 23 0 R
>>
endobj
